From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: preserve Cliffs controller GDSC parent regulator ownership

Use the exact Uke OEM MVS0C/MVS1C parent from MiCode DT 94c84aeb:
VDD_MM_MXC_VOTER_LEVEL votes MXC with the existing MMCX parent.
The native GDSC must enable this parent before controller clocks vote.
Require the bridge supply only for SM7675; keep other platforms unchanged.
This remains an inactive source candidate with no hardware acceptance.

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/videocc-sm8550.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/videocc-sm8550.c
@@ -673,6 +673,9 @@
 	}
 
 	if (is_sm7675) {
+		/* OEM MVSxC domains vote MXC with an MMCX parent before clocks. */
+		video_cc_mvs0c_gdsc.supply = "vdd_mm_mxc";
+		video_cc_mvs1c_gdsc.supply = "vdd_mm_mxc";
 		ret = uke_video_voltage_init(&pdev->dev);
 		if (ret)
 			return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, ret,
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,sm8450-videocc.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,sm8450-videocc.yaml
@@ -66,6 +66,9 @@
   vdd_mxc-supply:
     description: Aggregated MXC voltage-corner regulator for SM7675
 
+  vdd_mm_mxc-supply:
+    description: MXC regulator with MMCX parent for SM7675 controller power domains
+
 required:
   - compatible
   - clocks
@@ -94,6 +97,7 @@
       required:
         - vdd_mm-supply
         - vdd_mxc-supply
+        - vdd_mm_mxc-supply
       properties:
         power-domains: false
         required-opps: false
@@ -103,6 +107,7 @@
       properties:
         vdd_mm-supply: false
         vdd_mxc-supply: false
+        vdd_mm_mxc-supply: false
 
 unevaluatedProperties: false
 
